+## Manual prerequisite: valid RED before implementation
 
-The owner initializes a new state directory outside the worker worktree:
+Owner-directed correction, 2026-09-09. This prerequisite governs both
+direct implementation and dispatched work. It takes precedence over the
+older stage sequence below and conflicting test-role fallback or context
+instructions. It is an operating instruction, not a claim of a live guard.
 
-```sh
-python3 ops/conductor/tools/control.py init /absolute/plan.json --state /absolute/control-state
-```
+Work on one bounded acceptance behavior at a time:
+
+1. Name the declared requirement and the behavior the test must establish.
+   Test expectations do not create requirements or authorize contract changes.
+   Give the independent test producer the contract, established interfaces,
+   and relevant fixture context; independence must not require guessing at
+   existing behavior. Expectations remain grounded in the contract, not copied
+   from the candidate implementation.
+2. Assign independent test acceptance to a producer who authored neither the
+   tests nor their implementation; it must finish before implementation. The
+   implementation producer neither authors nor approves its acceptance tests.
+   Delegation uses the repository dispatch lane; no in-session fallback.
+3. Establish valid RED: verify fixture prerequisites and planted faults, run
+   the intended tests, and identify the assertion failing because the named
+   behavior is absent or wrong. Where existing behavior should work, include
+   a healthy control. Zero collected tests, collection/import errors and
+   unrelated setup failures are not valid RED. An assertion proving a missing
+   API establishes only that absence; it does not validate unreached assertions.
+4. Obtain independent acceptance of the tests and RED evidence. Before
+   authorizing implementation, the conductor retains the requirement
+   reference, fixture/control results, intended failure and command output,
+   source revision, exact test files and hashes, producer identities and the
+   independent acceptance record. Acceptance must cover these exact tests and
+   their RED evidence. Missing or contradictory evidence holds the affected
+   work; report expected, found and needed. Freeze the accepted test bytes.
+5. Implement and demonstrate GREEN with those unchanged tests and command.
+   If a test proves defective, stop the affected implementation, preserve the
+   attempt and return the test to an independent producer. Correct it, rerun
+   RED against the pre-fix source, obtain independent acceptance and freeze the
+   new version before resuming. Later evidence never validates an earlier
+   invalid sequence retroactively.
+6. Run required checks and bounded independent review, then open a draft PR
+   into dev. Keep the acceptance boundary fixed. Each added permanent test
+   must identify a distinct reachable failure and a gap in existing coverage;
+   prefer correcting or extending existing cases over duplicate inventories.
+
+Keep this evidence in the existing work record and PR evidence; this rule
+requires no new workflow engine or receipt framework. Independent examination
+must establish its meaning; a nonzero exit, approval label or pass count alone
+cannot do so.
 
